completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"In our exception handler, we try to determine if an exception is one thrown by a data store and if so, we want to return the response with a 503 status code, otherwise a 500 status code will suffice.\r\n\r\n```php\r\nfunction (\r\n    ServerRequestInterface $request,\r\n    ResponseInterface $response,\r\n    Throwable $exception\r\n): ResponseInterface {\r\n    if ($exception instanceof ElasticsearchException || $exception instanceof PDOException) {\r\n        return $response->withStatus(503);\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    return $response->withStatus(500);\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nIt generates the following error:\r\n\r\n```\r\nERROR: TypeDoesNotContainType - src/Infrastructure/Error/ErrorHandlerFactory.php:55:21 - Cannot resolve types for $exception - Throwable&Elasticsearch\\Common\\Exceptions\\ElasticsearchException does not contain PDOException\r\n```\r\n\r\nWeird thing is that if we switch the `instanceof` checks around, the error message remains identical, instead of indicating that `PDOException` does not contain `ElasticsearchException`.","closed_by":{"login":"muglug","id":2292638,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTI2Mzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2292638?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug","html_url":"https://github.com/muglug","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/muglug/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"